<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Harnett County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, November to December came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years, the most of any pair. In 2025 that same pair finished at 58% of normal, and in 2026 so far March to April sits at 33%. Grid 18506 had its driest year in 1986 at 68%, and a preliminary estimate there puts August to September 2026 at 55.8.</p>"}
